      "eyebrow": "Learn",
      "title": "Separate usage time from report time",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Deleted resources do not establish zero cost. Cost Explorer refreshes at least once every 24 hours; some data can take longer to appear.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "cost.residual_charge_verification"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "cost.residual_charge_verification#f1"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "cost.residual_charge_verification#tb1",
              "cost.residual_charge_verification#tb2"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Filter the supplied teardown interval by account and service or usage type. Compare usage timestamps with deletion evidence. Distinguish pre-deletion charges from continuing usage, then repeat after billing-data refresh rather than concluding from resource absence.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "cost.residual_charge_verification"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "cost.residual_charge_verification#f2",
              "cost.residual_charge_verification#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "cost.residual_charge_verification#tb3"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "data_table",
          "asset_ref": {
